  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 2,
    "summary": "A messianic psalm—The heathen will rage against the Lord’s anointed—The Lord speaks of His Son, whom He has begotten.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Why do the heathen rage, and the people imagine a vain thing?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 18,
            "text": "TG Heathen."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The kings of the earth set themselves, and the rulers take counsel together, against the Lord, and against his anointed, saying,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "Acts 4:26 (25–27)."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Counsel."
          },
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 119,
            "text": "TG Anointing."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 128
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let us break their bands asunder, and cast away their cords from us.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that sitteth in the heavens shall laugh: the Lord shall have them in derision.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Laughter."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Then shall he speak unto them in his wrath, and vex them in his sore displeasure.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Yet have I set my king upon my holy hill of Zion.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "HEB anointed my king."
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "Ps. 48:1; 99:9; Isa. 27:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I will declare the decree: the Lord hath said unto me, Thou art my Son; this day have I begotten thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 70,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Divine Sonship; Jesus Christ, Prophecies about."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Ask of me, and I shall give thee the heathen for thine inheritance, and the uttermost parts of the earth for thy possession.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 32
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          },
          {
            "start": 105,
            "end": 108
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou shalt break them with a rod of iron; thou shalt dash them in pieces like a potter’s vessel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "Isa. 11:4; 2 Ne. 21:4; D&C 19:15."
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "Rev. 2:27 (26–28)."
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "Isa. 30:14 (13–14)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be wise now therefore, O ye kings: be instructed, ye judges of the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Serve the Lord with fear, and rejoice with trembling.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Reverence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Kiss the Son, lest he be angry, and ye perish from the way, when his wrath is kindled but a little. Blessed are all they that put their trust in him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 100,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "TG Blessing."
          },
          {
            "start": 136,
            "end": 141,
            "text": "TG Trust in God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 50
          },
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 111
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
